{"schema":1,"fm":{"schema":1,"id":"write-mock-horoscopes","kind":"prompt","title":"Write mock horoscopes","description":"Writes twelve funny mock horoscopes themed to a workplace, club, school or event for a newsletter or party, clearly parody, with no real predictions about health, money or love.","category":"humor","version":"1.0.0","status":"incubating","stage":["build"],"role":["individual","manager","content-creator"],"requires":["none"],"inputs":["topic","text"],"output":["copy"],"risk":"read-only","invocation":"user","effort":"quick","interaction":"one-shot","model_tier":"mid","reasoning":"optional","level":"beginner","depth":"specific","tags":["newsletter-filler","parody","office-newsletter","star-signs","party-game"],"pairs_with":{"prompts":["write-clean-jokes","write-funny-awards-ceremony"]},"args":[{"name":"theme","description":"The world the horoscopes are set in and its shared references, for example \"a hospital ward newsletter - night shifts, the broken coffee machine, the new rota system\", \"a running club\", \"a sixth-form magazine\".","type":"text","required":true},{"name":"length","description":"Words per sign.","type":"number","default":40}],"output_contract":{"format":"markdown","sections":["Horoscopes","Disclaimer line"]},"authorship":"ai-assisted","authors":["gabrielanhaia"],"last_reviewed":"2026-10-11","changelog":[{"version":"1.0.0","note":"First version."}]},"body":"<context>\nYou write parody horoscopes for newsletters, magazines and parties. The comedy borrows the genre's voice (cosmic portent, planets \"entering\" things, vague advice, lucky numbers and colours) and applies it to the small dramas of a specific shared world: the meeting that runs over, the rota, the club's muddy kit. They work when every reader recognises the references and nobody can tell which colleague a sign is \"about\". They fail when they lean on star-sign stereotypes too hard, predict anything that sounds real (illness, breakups, money), or target someone.\n\nTheme: {{theme}}\nWords per sign: about {{length}}\n</context>\n\n<task>\n1. List 10 to 15 shared references from the theme that readers will recognise.\n2. Write a horoscope for each of the twelve signs in order (Aries to Pisces) with mock-cosmic language, one shared reference each, and a mock lucky item drawn from the theme (lucky number, colour or object).\n3. Vary the jokes: no two signs with the same structure or punchline.\n4. Add a one-line parody disclaimer in the same tone.\n</task>\n\n<constraints>\n- No predictions or advice about health, pregnancy, money, relationships, exams or job security, even jokingly.\n- Never make a sign identifiable as a real person.\n- Keep sign stereotypes light and secondary to the theme jokes.\n- Stay within about {{length}} words per sign.\n</constraints>\n\n<output_format>\n## Horoscopes\nTwelve entries: **Sign (dates):** text. Lucky item.\n## Disclaimer line\n</output_format>","steps":[]}
